/*  Functions as values — a function type, a named function passed or stored, `a function given
    (…): … Done.`, a `Bind` inside a body, and a call of any of them.

    ★ A function value is `{ fn, env }`: a C function taking the environment first, then its
      arguments, and the environment it was made with. Its kind is written `function(R;P1;P2)` —
      what it gives back, then what it takes — split as a record's parts are.

    ★ A named function used as a value goes through a THUNK, which drops the environment it never
      had. A lambda, or a `Bind` written inside a body, is a static C function of its own, and its
      environment holds what it captured — copied when it is made, as the language has it: a
      number, a text, a fact, an object is a snapshot, and a series or a map, held by its address,
      is the same series or map. Inside, a captured name reads through the environment, the way a
      narrowed name reads through its case (`@<name>`).

    ★ A `Bind` inside a body may call ITSELF: inside, its own name is the value made of its function
      and the environment it was given.

    ★ A lambda's result is worked out from its body — a first pass over it, in a writer of its own,
      notes what its first `Return` gives — and the second pass writes it.

    ⚠ An object holding a function waits: the function's struct comes after the objects.
*/

Pull a book on collections.
    Bind fact to is-function, given (the text kind):
        Return kind starts with "function(".
    Done.

    /// A function kind's parts — what it gives back, then what it takes — split outside brackets.
    Bind series of text to function-parts, given (the text kind):
        Define inner as the characters from 10 to (the length of kind - 1) of kind.
        Define parts as a series of text.
        Define depth as 0.
        Define begun as 1.
        Define place as 0.
        Define total as the length of inner.
        While place is less than total, repeat:
            Increment place by 1.
            Define letter as the characters from place to place of inner.
            If letter is "(", increment depth by 1.
            If letter is ")", decrement depth by 1.
            If letter is ";" and depth is 0:
                Insert (the characters from begun to (place - 1) of inner) into parts.
                The begun becomes place + 1.
            Done.
        Done.
        Insert (the characters from begun to total of inner) into parts.
        Return parts.
    Done.

    Bind text to function-gives, given (the text kind):
        Return item 1 of cast function-parts on (kind).
    Done.

    Bind series of text to function-takes, given (the text kind):
        Define taken as a series of text.
        Define place as 0.
        For each part in cast function-parts on (kind), repeat:
            Increment place by 1.
            If place is greater than 1, insert part into taken.
        Done.
        Return taken.
    Done.

    Bind text to function-kind-from, given (the text gives, the series of text takes):
        Define written as "function({gives}".
        For each part in takes, repeat:
            The written becomes "{written};{part}".
        Done.
        Return "{written})".
    Done.

    Bind text to function-c-name, given (the text kind):
        Define gives-tag as "void".
        If cast function-gives on (kind) is not "void", the gives-tag becomes cast c-tag on (cast function-gives on (kind)).
        Define named as "cfn_r{gives-tag}".
        For each part in cast function-takes on (kind), repeat:
            The named becomes "{named}_{cast c-tag on (part)}".
        Done.
        Return named.
    Done.

    /// The C type a function gives back — `void` for none.
    Bind text to c-gives, given (the text gives):
        If gives is "void", return "void".
        Return cast c-type on (gives).
    Done.

    /// Whether a function kind's struct can be written ahead of the objects, so an object may hold
    /// one: everything it takes and gives is named by then — a number, a text, a fact, or a series
    /// or map, held by its address.
    Bind fact to is-early-function, given (the text kind):
        Define parts as cast function-takes on (kind).
        Insert cast function-gives on (kind) into parts.
        For each part in parts, repeat:
            Define element as cast element-of on (part).
            Define named-ahead as cast is-scalar on (part) or part is "void" or cast is-map on (part)
                or cast is-scalar on (element) or (element is not "" and cast object-of on (element) is not "").
            If named-ahead is false, return false.
        Done.
        Return true.
    Done.

    /// A function kind's struct.
    Bind text to c-function-helpers, given (the text kind):
        Define param-list as "void*".
        For each part in cast function-takes on (kind), repeat:
            The param-list becomes "{param-list}, {cast c-type on (part)}".
        Done.
        Return "typedef struct \{ {cast c-gives on (cast function-gives on (kind))} (*fn)({param-list}); void* env; \} {cast function-c-name on (kind)};\n".
    Done.

    Bind void to register-function unto emitter, given (the text kind):
        If (the entry for kind in one's unions) is void:
            In one's unions, the entry for kind becomes true.
            Insert kind into one's union-order.
        Done.
    Done.

    /// The kind of a written function type.
    Bind text or failure to function-kind-of-type unto emitter, given (the node written):
        Define takes as a series of text.
        For each taken in (cast field-of on (written, 1))'s children, repeat:
            Define taken-kind as cast one's kind-of-type on (taken) or pass the failure off.
            Insert taken-kind into takes.
        Done.
        Define gives as "void".
        If (cast field-of on (written, 2))'s kind is not "VoidType":
            The gives becomes cast one's kind-of-type on (cast field-of on (written, 2)) or pass the failure off.
        Done.
        Define kind as cast function-kind-from on (gives, takes).
        Cast one's register-function on (kind).
        Return kind.
    Done.

    /// The kind a function declared with `Bind` has as a value.
    Bind text or failure to bound-kind unto emitter, given (the node bound):
        Define takes as a series of text.
        For each parameter in (cast field-of on (bound, 3))'s children, repeat:
            Define taken-kind as cast one's kind-of-type on (cast field-of on (parameter, 1)) or pass the failure off.
            Insert taken-kind into takes.
        Done.
        Define gives as cast one's kind-of-type on (cast field-of on (bound, 2)) or pass the failure off.
        Define kind as cast function-kind-from on (gives, takes).
        Cast one's register-function on (kind).
        Return kind.
    Done.

    // ── A named function as a value ───────────────────────────────────────

    /// A top-level function, as a value: through a thunk that drops the environment.
    Bind text or failure to c-named-function unto emitter, given (the text name):
        Define bound as the entry for name in one's functions but void is cast listed.
        Define kind as cast one's bound-kind on (bound) or pass the failure off.
        Define thunk as "cft_{cast c-ident on (name)}".
        If (the entry for "thunk:{name}" in one's unions) is void:
            In one's unions, the entry for "thunk:{name}" becomes true.
            Define param-list as "void* cf_env".
            Define passed as "".
            Define place as 0.
            For each part in cast function-takes on (kind), repeat:
                Increment place by 1.
                The param-list becomes "{param-list}, {cast c-type on (part)} cf_a{place}".
                If passed is not "", the passed becomes "{passed}, ".
                The passed becomes "{passed}cf_a{place}".
            Done.
            Define head as "static {cast c-gives on (cast function-gives on (kind))} {thunk}({param-list})".
            Insert "{head};\n" into one's lambda-protos.
            Define gives-back as "return ".
            If cast function-gives on (kind) is "void", the gives-back becomes "".
            Insert "{head} \{ (void)cf_env; {gives-back}{cast c-function-name on (name)}({passed}); \}\n\n" into one's lambda-code.
        Done.
        Return "(({cast function-c-name on (kind)})\{ {thunk}, NULL \})".
    Done.

    // ── Lambdas and a Bind inside a body ──────────────────────────────────

    /// The names a body reads that are NOT its own — what a function made here captures: each one
    /// this place knows that the body neither takes nor declares.
    Bind void to free-names unto emitter, given (the node tree, the map from text to fact own, the map from text to fact found):
        Define kind as tree's kind.
        If kind is "DefineStatement" or kind is "BindStatement", in own, the entry for cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (tree, 1)) becomes true.
        If kind is "ForEachStatement" and cast is-nothing on (cast field-of on (tree, 1)) is false:
            In own, the entry for cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (tree, 1)) becomes true.
        Done.
        If kind is "VariableReference":
            Define read as cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (tree, 1)).
            If (the entry for read in own) is void and (the entry for read in one's kinds) is not void, in found, the entry for read becomes true.
            Return.
        Done.
        For each child in tree's children, repeat:
            Cast one's free-names on (child, own, found).
        Done.
    Done.

    /// A function written here — `a function given (…): … Done.` or a `Bind` inside a body — built as
    /// a C function of its own, and the value that holds it and what it captured. `named` is the
    /// Bind's name, "" for a lambda; `gives` what it gives back, "?" to work it out from its body.
    Bind text or failure to c-closure unto emitter, given (the node parameters, the node body, the text named,
            the text gives, the text label):
        // Its parameters, and what it captures — every name the body reads that this place knows.
        Define takes as a series of text.
        Define taken-names as a series of text.
        Define own as a map from text to fact.
        For each parameter in parameters's children, repeat:
            Define taken-kind as cast one's kind-of-type on (cast field-of on (parameter, 1)) or pass the failure off.
            Insert taken-kind into takes.
            Define taken-name as cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (parameter, 2)).
            Insert taken-name into taken-names.
            In own, the entry for taken-name becomes true.
        Done.
        If named is not "", in own, the entry for named becomes true.
        Define found as a map from text to fact.
        For each statement in body's children, repeat:
            Cast one's free-names on (statement, own, found).
        Done.
        Define captured as a series of text.
        For each pair in found, repeat:
            If cast one's stored-kind on (the key of pair) is not "", insert the key of pair into captured.
        Done.
        Define env-type as "cenv_{label}".
        Define fn-name as "cf_lam_{label}".

        // What it gives back: written, or worked out by a first pass over the body.
        Define result as gives.
        If result is "?":
            Define trial as cast one's sibling.
            Cast trial's enter-closure on (takes, taken-names, captured, one's kinds, named, "?", label, fn-name, env-type).
            In one's inferred, the entry for label becomes "void".
            In one's inferred, the entry for "?{label}" becomes "".
            For each statement in body's children, repeat:
                Cast trial's emit-statement on (statement) or pass the failure off.
            Done.
            The result becomes the entry for label in one's inferred but void is "void".
        Done.
        Define kind as cast function-kind-from on (result, takes).
        Cast one's register-function on (kind).
        Define value-type as cast function-c-name on (kind).
        If named is "", in one's inferred, the entry for "λ{label}" becomes kind.

        // The environment, and the function — written once, with its own writer, however often
        // its kind or its C is asked for.
        If (the entry for "built:{label}" in one's inferred) is void:
            In one's inferred, the entry for "built:{label}" becomes "yes".
            Cast one's build-closure on (takes, taken-names, captured, named, result, label, fn-name, env-type, body) or pass the failure off.
        Done.

        // The value: an environment filled with what it captured, as it is now.
        Define filled as "{env-type}* cf_e = ({env-type}*)cufet_arena_alloc(sizeof({env-type})); memset(cf_e, 0, sizeof({env-type}));".
        For each name in captured, repeat:
            // Stored as it is stored here — read through this function's own environment, when it
            // was captured from further out too, and never as a narrowed case.
            Define captured-c as cast c-name on (name).
            // `one` is held by its address in a method; what is captured is the object, a snapshot.
            If name is "one", the captured-c becomes "(*cv_one)".
            Define redirected as the entry for "@{name}" in one's kinds but void is "".
            If redirected starts with "(cf_env->" or redirected starts with "((cfn_", the captured-c becomes redirected.
            The filled becomes "{filled} cf_e->{cast c-name on (name)} = {captured-c};".
        Done.
        Return "(\{ {filled} ({value-type})\{ {fn-name}, cf_e \}; \})".
    Done.

    /// The environment's struct and the C function, written once.
    Bind void or failure to build-closure unto emitter, given (the series of text takes, the series of text taken-names,
            the series of text captured, the text named, the text result, the text label, the text fn-name,
            the text env-type, the node body):
        Define fields as "char cf_nothing;".
        For each name in captured, repeat:
            The fields becomes "{fields} {cast c-type on (cast one's stored-kind on (name))} {cast c-name on (name)};".
        Done.
        Insert "typedef struct \{ {fields} \} {env-type};\n" into one's lambda-types.
        Define writer as cast one's sibling.
        Cast writer's enter-closure on (takes, taken-names, captured, one's kinds, named, result, label, fn-name, env-type).
        For each statement in body's children, repeat:
            Cast writer's emit-statement on (statement) or pass the failure off.
        Done.
        Cast writer's close-failable.
        Define param-list as "void* cf_envp".
        Define place as 0.
        For each taken in takes, repeat:
            Increment place by 1.
            The param-list becomes "{param-list}, {cast c-type on (taken)} {cast c-name on (item place of taken-names)}".
        Done.
        Define head as "static {cast c-gives on (result)} {fn-name}({param-list})".
        Insert "{head};\n" into one's lambda-protos.
        Insert "{head} \{\n    {env-type}* cf_env = ({env-type}*)cf_envp; (void)cf_env;\n{writer's body converted to text}\}\n\n" into one's lambda-code.
    Done.

    /// A writer's kinds set for a function written here: what it takes, what it captured — read
    /// through its environment — its own name, if it has one, and what it gives back.
    Bind void to enter-closure unto emitter, given (the series of text takes, the series of text taken-names,
            the series of text captured, the map from text to text outer, the text named, the text gives,
            the text label, the text fn-name, the text env-type):
        Cast one's line on ("int cf_ab = cufet_arena_top; int cf_fo = cufet_alloc_override; (void)cf_ab; (void)cf_fo;").
        For each name in captured, repeat:
            Define captured-kind as the entry for "%{name}" in outer but void is (the entry for name in outer but void is "").
            In one's kinds, the entry for name becomes captured-kind.
            In one's kinds, the entry for "%{name}" becomes captured-kind.
            In one's kinds, the entry for "@{name}" becomes "(cf_env->{cast c-name on (name)})".
        Done.
        Define place as 0.
        For each taken in takes, repeat:
            Increment place by 1.
            In one's kinds, the entry for item place of taken-names becomes taken.
        Done.
        In one's kinds, the entry for "%return" becomes gives.
        In one's kinds, the entry for "%closure" becomes label.
        If named is not "":
            Cast one's feed-stage on (named).
            Define self-kind as cast function-kind-from on (gives, takes).
            In one's kinds, the entry for named becomes self-kind.
            In one's kinds, the entry for "%{named}" becomes self-kind.
            In one's kinds, the entry for "@{named}" becomes "(({cast function-c-name on (self-kind)})\{ {fn-name}, cf_envp \})".
        Done.
    Done.

    /// While a lambda's result is worked out: what its first `Return` gives is noted.
    Bind text or failure to noted-return unto emitter, given (the node returned):
        Define label as the entry for "%closure" in one's kinds but void is "".
        Define returned-kind as cast one's kind-of on (returned) or pass the failure off.
        If (the entry for "?{label}" in one's inferred but void is "") is "":
            In one's inferred, the entry for label becomes returned-kind.
            In one's inferred, the entry for "?{label}" becomes "noted".
        Done.
        Return cast one's c-of on (returned) or pass the failure off.
    Done.

    /// `Bind … given (…): … Done.` inside a body — a local name holding the function it makes.
    Bind void or failure to emit-local-bind unto emitter, given (the node statement):
        If the number of statement's children is greater than 8, return a failure (cast not-built on ("a Bind with {(cast field-of on (statement, 9))'s word} inside a body")).
        Define name as cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (statement, 1)).
        Define gives as cast one's kind-of-type on (cast field-of on (statement, 2)) or pass the failure off.
        Define label as "{(cast field-of on (statement, 7))'s word}_{(cast field-of on (statement, 8))'s word}".
        Define value as cast one's c-closure on (cast field-of on (statement, 3), cast field-of on (statement, 4), name, gives, label) or pass the failure off.
        Define kind as cast one's bound-kind on (statement) or pass the failure off.
        In one's kinds, the entry for name becomes kind.
        In one's kinds, the entry for "%{name}" becomes kind.
        In one's kinds, the entry for "@{name}" becomes "".
        Cast one's declared-here on (name).
        Cast one's line on ("{cast function-c-name on (kind)} {cast c-name on (name)} = {value};").
    Done.

    /// `a function given (…): … Done.` — its kind, and its C.
    Bind text or failure to lambda-kind unto emitter, given (the node expression):
        Define label as "{(cast field-of on (expression, 3))'s word}_{(cast field-of on (expression, 4))'s word}".
        Define known as the entry for "λ{label}" in one's inferred but void is "".
        If known is not "", return known.
        Cast one's c-closure on (cast field-of on (expression, 1), cast field-of on (expression, 2), "", "?", label) or pass the failure off.
        Return the entry for "λ{label}" in one's inferred but void is "".
    Done.

    // ── Calling a function value ──────────────────────────────────────────

    /// Whether a call reaches a function VALUE rather than a function or a method by its name.
    Bind fact or failure to calls-value unto emitter, given (the node call):
        Define callee as cast field-of on (call, 1).
        If callee's kind is "VariableReference":
            If (the entry for cast call-target on (call) in one's functions) is not void, return false.
            Define called-name as cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (callee, 1)).
            Return cast is-function on (cast one's stored-kind on (called-name)).
        Done.
        If callee's kind is "PossessiveAccess":
            Define owner-kind as cast one's kind-of on (cast field-of on (callee, 1)) or pass the failure off.
            Define owner as cast object-of on (owner-kind).
            If owner is not "" and (the entry for "{owner}'s {cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (callee, 2))}" in one's methods) is not void, return false.
        Done.
        Define callee-kind as cast one's kind-of on (callee) but on failure "".
        Return cast is-function on (callee-kind).
    Done.

    /// A call of a function value, as C: through its function, with its environment first.
    Bind text or failure to c-value-call unto emitter, given (the node call):
        Define callee as cast field-of on (call, 1).
        Define kind as cast one's kind-of on (callee) or pass the failure off.
        Define callee-c as cast one's c-of on (callee) or pass the failure off.
        Define takes as cast function-takes on (kind).
        Define operands as a series of node.
        Define emitted as a series of text.
        Define place as 0.
        For each argument in (cast field-of on (call, 2))'s children, repeat:
            Increment place by 1.
            Define argument-c as cast one's c-of-as on (argument, item place of takes) or pass the failure off.
            Insert argument into operands.
            Insert argument-c into emitted.
        Done.
        Define prefix as cast order-prefix on (operands, emitted).
        Define param-list as "cf_fv.env".
        For each argument-c in emitted, repeat:
            The param-list becomes "{param-list}, {argument-c}".
        Done.
        Return "(\{ {cast function-c-name on (kind)} cf_fv = {callee-c}; {cast in-order on (prefix, "cf_fv.fn({param-list})")}; \})".
    Done.
Done.
